From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 13:56:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 162/162] PC5: the controllers a game starts with don't tell
 its windows that devices changed (Wine patch 1035)

The controller the player holds when the game starts was counted as a connect, so every game with a controller got WM_DEVICECHANGE (DBT_DEVNODES_CHANGED, no data) at its first window, which Windows never sends; a game that reads the message's data crashed at once. The controllers connected at the driver's first look are now where its count starts, and only a connect or disconnect after that is announced.
---
 ...ame-starts-with-are-no-device-change.patch | 53 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 53 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 wine/patches/1035-win32u-ps5-the-controllers-a-game-starts-with-are-no-device-change.patch

diff --git a/wine/patches/1035-win32u-ps5-the-controllers-a-game-starts-with-are-no-device-change.patch b/wine/patches/1035-win32u-ps5-the-controllers-a-game-starts-with-are-no-device-change.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..f1614a8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/wine/patches/1035-win32u-ps5-the-controllers-a-game-starts-with-are-no-device-change.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,53 @@
+From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
+Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 14:00:00 +0000
+Subject: [PATCH] win32u: PS5: the controllers a game starts with are no device change.
+
+Patch 0984 posts WM_DEVICECHANGE with DBT_DEVNODES_CHANGED to every
+top-level window when the title's controller connects or disconnects.
+Its count of changes starts at 0, and the controller the player holds
+when the game starts is its first connect, so every game with a
+controller got the message at its first window, when Windows sends
+nothing. GIGASWORD's window reads the message's data, which
+DBT_DEVNODES_CHANGED doesn't have (lParam 0), and crashed at once,
+reading address 0, in both graphics modes.
+
+The count at the driver's first look is now where it starts: the
+controllers connected then are the ones the game starts with, and only
+a connect or disconnect after that is announced, as Windows announces a
+device added or removed while a program runs. A game whose controller
+goes off and comes back while it runs (the Unreal Engine 4 game patch
+0984 was made for) is told, as before.
+---
+ dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c | 12 +++++++++---
+ 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)
+
+diff --git a/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c b/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
+index 904b854..898fd92 100644
+--- a/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
++++ b/dlls/win32u/ps5drv.c
+@@ -1010,15 +1010,21 @@ static BOOL dialog_key( HWND hwnd, const struct ps5_input *event )
+  * (pw_wine_pad_changes). Windows then tells every top-level window that
+  * devices changed, through the plug and play service a title cannot run.
+  * Some games (Unreal Engine 4) only look for a lost XInput controller
+- * again when told. */
++ * again when told. The controllers connected at the first look are the
++ * ones the game starts with, which Windows announces to no one: counted as
++ * a change, they told every game at its first window that devices changed,
++ * and one that reads the message's data without checking for it crashed. */
+ static void notify_pad_changes(void)
+ {
+     static UINT32 seen;
+-    UINT32 changes;
++    static LONG looked;
++    UINT32 changes, before;
+ 
+     if (!pad_changes) return;
+     changes = pad_changes();
+-    if (__atomic_exchange_n( &seen, changes, __ATOMIC_RELAXED ) == changes) return;
++    before = __atomic_exchange_n( &seen, changes, __ATOMIC_RELAXED );
++    if (!__atomic_exchange_n( &looked, 1, __ATOMIC_RELAXED )) return;
++    if (before == changes) return;
+     TRACE( "controller connected or disconnected (%u): WM_DEVICECHANGE\n", changes );
+     NtUserPostMessage( HWND_BROADCAST, WM_DEVICECHANGE, DBT_DEVNODES_CHANGED, 0 );
+ }
